        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe new `CapMembershipLevel` function itself is idiomatic \u2014 it mirrors `CountHouseholdMembers` precisely (same `@Val Owner` + `OwnerRepository.findAll()` loop, mutate-in-place, store a create-time value on the entity that `MembershipLevel` later consumes). Persisting `membershipLevelCap` as a column alongside `householdMemberCount`/`namesakeCount` and applying it in `MembershipLevel.of` (the \"single source of truth\") are both consistent with the existing design. So the additive part is fine.\n\nThe problem is a non-additive, unrelated deletion bundled into this change:\n\n- **The `checkHousehold` step (`CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique`) was removed from `owners.POST.yml`.** This silently drops the household duplicate-detection behavior (the 409 for an undeclared second member of a household) that has nothing to do with the membership-cap spec. A maintainer reviewing \"add a membership-level cap\" would not expect household uniqueness enforcement to disappear. If this removal is genuinely required, it needs to be its own change with its own justification; it should not ride along inside this feature.\n\n- **The removal leaves dead code.** `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique.java` is now wired into no pipeline, and its escalation handler (`officefloor/escalation/...OwnerHouseholdDuplicateException.yml`) plus `OwnerHouseholdDuplicateException` are now unreachable. Either the step should stay wired, or the orphaned class/handler/exception should be deleted so the codebase stays coherent \u2014 leaving them stranded is exactly the kind of drift a maintainer would find unnatural.\n\nRecommendation: restore the `checkHousehold` step (keep the diff purely additive \u2014 insert `capMembershipLevel` after `countHousehold` without touching the earlier wiring), or, if dropping household uniqueness is actually intended, split it into a separate, justified change and remove the now-dead class, handler, and exception along with it.\n\nOne minor, non-blocking note: the household-membership iteration (`findAll()` + filter by `householdId`) is now triplicated across `CountHouseholdMembers`, `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique`, and `CapMembershipLevel`. That duplication predates this change and each copy has a distinct purpose, so it's consistent with the existing style \u2014 but if a shared helper (e.g. on `OwnerHousehold`) is ever introduced, this new call site should use it too."
